{
    "_notes": "FIFO-enabled 6-axis IMU. FIFO continuous mode at matched sensor ODR. FIFO depth is LIMITED to the watermark (FIFO_CTRL4.STOP_ON_FTH=1, FTH=1020 words via FIFO_CTRL1/2) so DIFF_FIFO can never wrap to 0: with an unlimited depth a host pause of >6.6 s (e.g. an RSAO test-mode or commissioning session) filled the 4096-word FIFO, the count read 0 and the {$0.w12} poll read nothing forever (devdocs/lsm6ds-fifo-full-deadlock.md, 2026-09-11). Two-phase I2C read: first reads FIFO_STATUS1-4 (word count), then reads only the required FIFO data bytes from 0x3E. FIFO_PATTERN (STATUS3/4) used to skip to next aligned group boundary before decoding. Each sample = 6 words (gx,gy,gz,ax,ay,az). Detection: WHO_AM_I 0x6A (LSM6DSL, LSM6DSM, LSM6DS3TR-C) and 0x69 (LSM6DS3, LSM6DS33). On 0x69 parts STOP_ON_FTH is CTRL4_C bit 0, not FIFO_CTRL4 bit 7, so the FIFO-full protection doesn't take effect there (they poll normally; a long host pause can still fill the FIFO) - they need a record of their own. 0x6C parts (LSM6DSO/DSOX/DSO32) have a different FIFO and aren't matched. The _conf.rate entries keep the 1020-word watermark.",
